# A registry entry can limit the calls of a service (may_call) and its
# callers (called_by). SV111 reports a call that a limit refuses.
exits 1 sv check specs/limits.yaml
cmp stdout limits.txt

# SR005 reports a limit that is not a list, or a value that is not a layer or
# a registered service. SR006 warns about a limit that permits more than the
# layer rules.
cd $WORK/badlimits
exits 1 sv check
cmp stdout $WORK/badlimits.txt

-- .specval.yaml --
-- .specval/data/services.yaml --
services:
  OrderManager: { layer: manager }
  PricingEngine: { layer: engine, called_by: [OrderManager] }
  BillingManager: { layer: manager }
  ConfigUtility: { layer: utility, may_call: [] }
  LogUtility: { layer: utility }
-- specs/limits.yaml --
specval: 1
id: LIM-1
kind: feature
title: Limits
summary: The calls test the limits of the registry.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: "Given an order, when it is priced, then the price is logged." }
calls:
  - { from: OrderManager, to: PricingEngine, op: Price, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: BillingManager, to: PricingEngine, op: Price, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: LogUtility, to: ConfigUtility, op: Read, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: ConfigUtility, to: LogUtility, op: Write, covers: [AC1] }
-- limits.txt --
specs/limits.yaml:10 error SV111 BillingManager cannot call PricingEngine, because called_by of PricingEngine in the registry does not permit it (calls[1])
    fix: PricingEngine can be called only by OrderManager. Change the call, or ask the owners of the registry to change called_by of PricingEngine.
specs/limits.yaml:12 error SV111 ConfigUtility cannot call LogUtility, because may_call of ConfigUtility in the registry does not permit it (calls[3])
    fix: ConfigUtility has an empty may_call. Remove the call, or ask the owners of the registry to change may_call of ConfigUtility.
specval checked 1 spec(s) and found 2 error(s) and 0 warning(s).
-- badlimits/.specval.yaml --
-- badlimits/.specval/data/services.yaml --
services:
  OrderManager: { layer: manager }
  ConfigUtility: { layer: utility, may_call: [manager, Nobody] }
  LogUtility: { layer: utility, called_by: OrderManager }
-- badlimits.txt --
.specval/data/services.yaml:3 error SR005 "Nobody" in may_call of ConfigUtility is not a layer or a registered service (services.ConfigUtility.may_call[1])
    fix: Use a layer (client, manager, engine, accessor, resource, utility) or a registered service.
.specval/data/services.yaml:3 warning SR006 may_call of ConfigUtility has manager, but the layer rules do not permit a call from a utility to a manager (services.ConfigUtility.may_call[0])
    fix: Remove manager from may_call. A limit can only make the layer rules stricter.
.specval/data/services.yaml:4 error SR005 called_by of LogUtility is not a list (got "OrderManager") (services.LogUtility.called_by)
    fix: Write called_by as a list of layers and services, for example [manager, OrderManager].
specval checked 0 spec(s) and found 2 error(s) and 1 warning(s).
